&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Data Science, Information Systems, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of software engineering, data engineering, search, document-processing, or related experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python development experience and experience building production-grade data or content-processing pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience processing PDFs, images, scanned documents, and semi-structured content using OCR and document-extraction technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with document stores, search engines, or vector databases, including embeddings and semantic retrieval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with document parsing, classification, chunking, metadata enrichment, and preservation of source provenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;LLM-enabled or agentic document-processing workflows&lt;/strong&gt;, including extraction, validation, routing, or exception handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building robust pipelines with automated testing, logging, monitoring, error handling, and quality controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating OCR and extraction quality using measurable criteria and confidence thresholds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills for working with complex and inconsistent document formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;OpenSearch&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS document-processing, AI, or machine-learning services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;agentic frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, or similar orchestration frameworks&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multimodal models, vision-language models, or LLM-based document extraction.&lt;/li&gt;
