&lt;h2 class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: large;&quot;&gt;Overview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black Canyon Consulting &lt;strong&gt;(BCC)&lt;/strong&gt; is searching for a&lt;strong&gt; Database Architect with expertise in Cloud Technologies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to support National Center for Biotechnology Information&lt;strong&gt; (NCBI), &lt;/strong&gt;part of the U.S. National Library of Medicine, National Institutes of Health.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;c-message__edited_label&quot;&gt;This opportunity is full time and onsite at the NCBI in Bethesda, MD.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Database Architecture will design, optimize, and maintain large-scale, distributed database systems powering NCBI’s premier biomedical data resources. This role focuses on scalable database architectures, partitioning strategies, and cloud-native solutions to support massive, complex datasets driving global biomedical and public health research.&lt;span class=&quot;c-message__edited_label&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
