&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is part of the National Library of Medicine (NLM) at&amp;nbsp;the National Institutes of Health (NIH).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov%2F&amp;amp;data=02%7C01%7Cmanish.salhotra%40mscweb.com%7C13529751b18c41b1bfc808d7c6c1bfec%7Cb8c50eab690d48e8a21a9d57df50c57c%7C0%7C0%7C637196407765646372&amp;amp;sdata=2J5aoI08leFUY%2FxyQYeXn7MkVznlUyqDU8xYHxVRzzs%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;NCBI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;is the world’s premier biomedical center hosting over six million daily users that seek research, clinical, genetic, and other information that directly impacts biomedical research and public health – at NCBI you can literally help to accelerate cures for diseases!&amp;nbsp;NCBI’s wide range of applications, platforms (node, python, Django, C++, you name it) and environments (big data [petabytes], machine learning, multiple clouds) serve more users than almost any other US Government Agency according to&lt;span class=&quot;apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fanalytics.usa.gov%2F&amp;amp;data=02%7C01%7Cmanish.salhotra%40mscweb.com%7C13529751b18c41b1bfc808d7c6c1bfec%7Cb8c50eab690d48e8a21a9d57df50c57c%7C0%7C0%7C637196407765646372&amp;amp;sdata=bbVeUkZMcMfJcForV%2Bwar%2F068L%2BgOQAqUIua%2BmbKdf0%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;https://analytics.usa.gov/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We attract the best people in the business with our competitive benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision coverage, 401k plan with employer contribution, paid holidays, vacation, and tuition reimbursement. If you enjoy being a part of a high performing, professional service and technology focused organization, please apply today!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: large;&quot;&gt;Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Support internal staff having desktop system and application issues via online ticketing systems &lt;br&gt;• Work in a dynamic environment supporting 700 users in a Windows OS based environment &lt;br&gt;• Help desk phone support and in person support &lt;br&gt;• Imaging new machines, installing and updating software &lt;br&gt;• Assist with the patching process as determined by the patch coordinator &lt;br&gt;• Remediate vulnerabilities flagged by the security team &lt;br&gt;• Prepare old computers for surplus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Provide OS X support to NCBI&#39;s internal developers and researchers&lt;br&gt;• Provision and deploy Mac endpoints for users&lt;br&gt;• Assist with deploying applications, updates (patch management), packaging, OS upgrades, hardware upgrades, etc.&lt;br&gt;• Help integrate macOS with network storage (SMB, NFS) and internal/external sites, including troubleshooting&lt;br&gt;• Install, configure and maintain mobile devices via Mobile Device Management software&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: small;&quot;&gt;Required Skills:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 3+ years experience&lt;br&gt;• High School Diploma/GED with either technical training/certifications, or equivalent experience&lt;br&gt;• Basic troubleshooting and problem-solving abilities&lt;br&gt;• Good communication, documentation, and customer service skills&lt;br&gt;• Experience with basic Unix command Line: file system navigation, ssh, rsync, chown, chmod, etc.&lt;br&gt;• Understanding of Apple technologies: packages, Installer, Device Enrollment Program, Apple Business Manager, Volume Purchase Program, Xcode and command line tool deployment, et. al.&lt;br&gt;• Enterprise experience: familiarity and experience with binding to Active Directory, AD/Mac integration, NoMAD, Microsoft Remote Desktop&lt;br&gt;• Mac Office suite and Exchange/Office 365 email and calendaring&lt;br&gt;• Familiarity with deploying and updating Adobe products&lt;br&gt;• Familiarity with CUPS and printer configuration and deployment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Familiarity with Jamf Pro (Jamf certifications a plus)&lt;br&gt;• Apple Certified Support Professional certification&lt;br&gt;• Scripting knowledge (bash, python)&lt;br&gt;• Knowledge of Smart Cards&lt;br&gt;• Willingness to learn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: large;&quot;&gt;Overview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We design and build medical devices. The engineering team is small, which means you&#39;ll own real work early and see your designs go into products that reach patients.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;d own the digital logic and board-level hardware side of our systems. Our embedded software lead handles Linux, device drivers, and application code. You won&#39;t be asked to do everything. You&#39;d be the hardware half of a two-person core.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One thing we want to be upfront about:&lt;/strong&gt; our advanced FPGA development is currently done by an engineering partner firm. We intend to bring that work in-house, and this role is how we do it. You&#39;d start by working alongside their engineers and grow into owning it over your first year or two. This process involves reading their designs, contributing to those designs and learning the architecture. This is a funded, planned transition, and the partner firm knows and supports it. They&#39;ll continue working with us on other projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That means we&#39;re not expecting you to walk in and architect an FPGA on day one. We&#39;re looking for someone with strong fundamentals who wants to grow into that ownership with real support while doing it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;d actually do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and verify synthesizable HDL, and close timing on real designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draw board-level schematics for FPGA-centric hardware: component selection, power architecture, clock distribution, peripheral and memory interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring boards up on the bench and debug what doesn&#39;t work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a layout engineer on stack-up and routing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write Python to automate hardware testing so we stop doing it by hand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to design documentation and verification within our quality system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow into architectural ownership of our FPGA designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we need you to have done already&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2–4 years of hands-on embedded or digital design work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Written HDL that went somewhere real.&lt;/strong&gt; Verilog, SystemVerilog, or VHDL. You&#39;ve simulated it, synthesized it, and dealt with timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Used an FPGA toolchain end-to-end.&lt;/strong&gt; We use Xilinx and Vivado. If your experience is Intel/Quartus, Lattice, or something else, the fundamentals transfer and we&#39;ll get you up to speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drawn a schematic yourself.&lt;/strong&gt; Altium, KiCad, OrCAD, whatever. We mean designed a board, not reviewed someone else&#39;s.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Written C, C++, or Rust (preferred)&lt;/strong&gt; at a low level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt; for scripting and data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort with an oscilloscope and a logic analyzer.&lt;/strong&gt; You should be the kind of engineer who reaches for a probe before a forum post.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SPI, I2C, and UART and their FPGA implementations (IP Block or hand coded HDL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of DSP, DDR interfaces, or high-speed signal integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Helpful, but genuinely not required&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We don&#39;t expect any one candidate to have all of these. Tell us which ones you have and we&#39;ll take it from there.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Xilinx Vivado/Vitis specifically, or AXI interconnect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zynq, MPSoC, or SoC design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Precision analog front-ends, ADCs, DACs, power management ICs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a regulated environment: medical, aerospace, automotive safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kernel driver experience. Take a hardware design and implement a Linux kernel driver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who does well here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Someone who&#39;s honest about the edges of what they know. Someone who&#39;d rather ask a question than guess. Someone who&#39;s willing to do the unglamorous parts: writing the test fixture, updating the schematic, and documenting the design. These are the things that allow the hardware to enter production and actually ship.&lt;br&gt;If you&#39;re strong in one area and thin in another, apply anyway and tell us which is which.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;How to apply&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Attach your resume, plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;a few paragraphs describing one hardware or HDL problem you personally debugged.&lt;/strong&gt; Tell us&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What was broken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How you found it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What you changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;We care more about that than a skills list. If you have a GitHub, a portfolio, or a project writeup, include it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
