&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in health informatics, biomedical terminology, terminology systems, interoperability, or a closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of UMLS and/or comparable biomedical terminology resources and their use in Health IT environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate complex technical and terminology concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Knowledge / Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with terminology modeling, mappings, FHIR, APIs, controlled vocabularies, ontologies, or Health IT interoperability standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with terminology consumers, developers, informaticians, data architects, researchers, or healthcare technology organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Education&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced education in health informatics, biomedical informatics, information science, computer science, biomedical science, healthcare, or a related field, or equivalent specialized experience.&lt;/p&gt;
