&lt;h2&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Lead Data Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to design and implement the core analytical data platform for a federal permitting modernization initiative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Lead Data Engineer will establish a modern lakehouse environment using &lt;strong&gt;DuckDB, Apache Iceberg, Amazon S3, and AWS Glue Catalog&lt;/strong&gt; and will lead the engineering patterns used to ingest, harmonize, and serve data across multiple source systems. The role will also help implement metadata-driven and agentic approaches to data engineering, including source analysis, mapping, pipeline generation, testing, reconciliation, and quality assurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on technical leadership role with responsibility for guiding and reviewing the work of other Data Engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is remote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement the core DuckDB / Apache Iceberg data platform on AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define physical data organization, schema, partitioning, file layout, snapshot, compaction, and optimization strategies for Iceberg tables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate DuckDB with Amazon S3, Apache Iceberg, and AWS Glue Catalog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish bronze, silver, and gold data-layer conventions and reusable engineering patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor Data Engineers, providing technical direction, code reviews, and engineering guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain analytical datasets supporting application services, reporting, analytics, and data science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reusable patterns for incremental loads, CDC, schema evolution, late-arriving data, backfills, and historical reconstruction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Data Architect to implement the common canonical data model and source-to-canonical mappings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead migration and harmonization of datasets from multiple source systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement reconciliation processes that demonstrate completeness and accuracy between source and target systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish automated data-quality monitoring, operational observability, and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement agentic and AI-enabled data engineering patterns supporting activities such as source analysis, mapping, pipeline generation, troubleshooting, reconciliation, and quality assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support integration of structured data with associated document and geospatial datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead development of certified data products, analytical datasets, and business metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize DuckDB queries and Iceberg datasets for performance and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop engineering documentation, operational procedures, and technical handoff materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Data Engineering, Information Systems, Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of relevant data engineering or data platform experience, including experience leading or mentoring other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience with &lt;strong&gt;DuckDB and Apache Iceberg&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL and strong Python development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building cloud-based analytical platforms using object storage and columnar formats such as Parquet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of partitioning, schema evolution, snapshots, compaction, incremental processing, and analytical query optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing bronze/silver/gold or comparable layered data architectures and transforming heterogeneous enterprise datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS data services, particularly Amazon S3 and AWS Glue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing reusable, metadata-driven ingestion and transformation frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing automated data quality, reconciliation, monitoring, and operational controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;agentic or AI-enabled data engineering solutions&lt;/strong&gt;, including the use of agents or AI-assisted workflows for activities such as data mapping, pipeline generation, validation, testing, or troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with agentic frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, or similar frameworks for building tool-using or multi-step AI workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting, performance tuning, and technical leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kafka or Amazon MSK and CDC architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GeoParquet, PostGIS, or geospatial datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with OpenSearch, document stores, or vector search technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating enterprise SaaS platforms, APIs, databases, and file-based sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in the &lt;strong&gt;U.S. Federal Government space&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with permitting, regulatory, land management, environmental, energy, or natural-resource datasets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits and Salary&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We attract the best people in the business with our competitive benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision coverage, 401k plan with employer contribution, paid holidays, vacation, and tuition reimbursement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy being a part of a high performing, professional service and technology focused organization, please apply today!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: large;&quot;&gt;Overview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black Canyon Consulting &lt;strong&gt;(BCC)&lt;/strong&gt; is actively looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Mid-Level C++ Developer &lt;/strong&gt;to support our work for the National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) at the National Library of Medicine (NLM), an institute of the National Institutes of Health. &lt;span class=&quot;c-message__edited_label&quot;&gt;This opportunity is full time and onsite at the NIH-NCBI in Bethesda, MD and/or remote work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;NCBI offers an intellectually stimulating environment where scientists, software developers, and other professionals work together to solve challenging problems and help accelerate the development of treatments and cures.&amp;nbsp;NCBI is a leading biomedical information center. It provides more than 6 million users each day with research, clinical, genetic, and other information that&amp;nbsp;supports biomedical research and public health.&amp;nbsp;NCBI uses a wide range of applications and technologies, including Node.js, Python, Django, and C++. Its environments include petabyte-scale data,&amp;nbsp;machine learning, and multiple cloud platforms. According to &lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;analytics.usa.gov&lt;/span&gt;, NCBI serves more users than almost any other U.S. government agency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The developer will join an NCBI dbSNP engineering team. The team builds and maintains high-performance software, back-end services, APIs, command-line tools, data-processing workflows, and selected web applications that support public biomedical data resources.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Role Summary&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;This role focuses mainly on C++ development, with significant use of Python. The developer will work on back-end services, data pipelines, APIs,&amp;nbsp;command-line tools, database interactions, and software that supports public-facing NCBI variation resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;This is not a front-end web developer position; However, the developer should be comfortable contributing to back-end web development. The developer&amp;nbsp;should also have experience with Python and Django web applications or be willing to learn them, especially for back-end work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Develop and maintain high-performance C++ programs, including public-facing services that use RESTful APIs, gRPC, and similar technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Develop and maintain internal command-line applications and libraries written in C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Write unit tests for C++ code using or Google Test. &lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;Boost.Test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Build and support Python packages, command-line tools, web services, and web applications with user interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Work with a variety of data sources, including relational databases, Cassandra keystores, and Solr collections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Maintain existing web application interfaces using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Make sure web applications are accessible and mobile-friendly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Develop and maintain test suites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Monitor applications for performance, security, and accessibility compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Work closely with an agile team that shares knowledge and responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Contribute to development standards, code reviews, and team process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science or a scientific field, such as engineering or physics, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;At least three years of &lt;strong&gt;professional &lt;/strong&gt;experience developing high-performance programs in C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience writing unit and integration tests for C++ systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;At least one year of &lt;strong&gt;professional&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;experience developing programs or libraries in Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;An understanding of accessibility and security compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience with version control systems such as Git or SVN.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;The ability to work well as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Desired Skills and Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience working with Hadoop and related big data technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience writing unit tests for Python code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience developing Django web applications and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience working with JavaScript frameworks such as Angular or React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience using web services and RESTful APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
