&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black Canyon Consulting &lt;strong&gt;(BCC)&lt;/strong&gt; is searching for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt; Senior Cloud Systems Administrator&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to join an established team of cloud professionals supporting high-throughput scientific computing and enterprise applications for the National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) at the National Library of Medicine (NLM), an institute of the National Institutes of Health. This opportunity is full time at the NCBI in Bethesda, MD.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will design, automate, manage, and optimize production multi-cloud environments across Google Cloud Platform (GCP) and Amazon Web Services (AWS). We are seeking a self-sufficient administrator with deep Unix/Linux systems administration experience who can manage production cloud infrastructure from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;CloudAdmin-Responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-Cloud Administration: Design, administer, and maintain world-class environments across Google Cloud Platform (GCP) and Amazon Web Services (AWS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as Code (IaC): Author, test, review, and maintain modular infrastructure code using Terraform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud Networking &amp;amp; Security: Design and maintain VPCs, subnets, routing tables, security groups, firewall rules, and hybrid interconnects ensuring compliance with federal security standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring &amp;amp; Observability: Implement and maintain telemetry, dashboards, and alerting across AWS CloudWatch/CloudTrail and GCP Cloud Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations &amp;amp; Troubleshooting: Provide support for multi-cloud infrastructure, including responding to security incidents, performance monitoring, and tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;CloudAdmin-RequiredQualifications&quot;&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of dedicated, hands-on enterprise Unix/Linux systems administration experience, with deep technical proficiency in systems internals, networking protocols, filesystems, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of direct operational experience administering production workloads in Amazon Web Services (AWS) or Google Cloud Platform (GCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, demonstrated proficiency in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform and git.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency with Kubernetes, including multi-cloud and cloud/on-prem hybrid environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical working knowledge of configuration management using Puppet (manifests, module structure, and Hiera) for systems integration and node provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-throughput web services, including HTTP/S internals, request flows, caching semantics, and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scripting and automation skills in Python and Bash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to operate independently and collaboratively in a team of senior cloud administrators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;CloudAdmin-DesiredQualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical operational familiarity with Alma Linux 8 or similar distributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing cloud environments in federal or biomedical research contexts subject to NIST / FedRAMP security frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;StandardFullstackdeveloperpositiondescriptionSenior-Requiredskillsandexperience&quot;&gt;Benefits and Salary&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We attract the best people in the business with our competitive benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision coverage, 401k plan with employer contribution, paid holidays, vacation, and tuition reimbursement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a competitive salary commensurate with experience and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy being a part of a high performing, professional service and technology focused organization, please apply today!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black Canyon Consulting (BCC) is searching for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Data Analyst&lt;/strong&gt;. The Senior Data Analyst will provide analytical leadership to develop a comprehensive strategic plan report that demonstrates impact and surfaces gaps to address during the next strategic plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The immediate and primary assignment is to lead&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;day-to-day development of a comprehensive 10-year summary report covering the 2017-2027 Strategic Plan&lt;/strong&gt;. This summary will not only serve as a record of NLM’s progress under the current strategic plan, but it will be used as an evidence input for development of the next strategic plan. Evidence of implementation and results is dispersed across OSI and NLM sources and was not organized through a single, systematic strategic-plan reporting process. The Senior Data Analyst will establish the report&#39;s evidence framework; inventory, organize, and synthesize existing information; assess evidence quality and limitations; conduct appropriate analyses; and develop leadership-ready findings, visualizations, and narrative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Data Analyst will work under OSI federal direction and collaborate with OSI staff and NLM Divisions, Offices, and Centers. This employee will lead the day-to-day analytical and production work, while OSI federal staff will establish strategic direction and retain responsibility for official institutional judgments, characterization of NLM&#39;s progress, and final approval of the report.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just as importantly, this person will help prepare for the next strategic plan by developing the systems, processes, and governance mechanisms needed to continuously measure progress and capture evidence throughout the life of the 2028-2032 strategic plan once it is implemented. Components may include an evidence and source catalog, goal-to-evidence crosswalks, structured repositories or data models, metadata and documentation standards, refresh and validation workflows, and reusable reports, dashboards, or query tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time opportunity supporting NLM in Bethesda, Maryland. The desired start date is immediately, subject to contract authorization and candidate availability, for a 12-month period of performance aligned with fiscal year 2027..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the day-to-day project and analytic lead, under OSI federal direction, for development of the 2017-2027 Strategic Plan Summary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage the report workplan, evidence framework, source inventory, goal- and objective-to-evidence crosswalk, analytical plan, outline, schedule, review process, and final production workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize existing information from disparate administrative, scientific, financial, workforce, operational, programmatic, and evaluation sources; use existing evidence as the default and limit new data calls to targeted follow-up needed to validate or clarify information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize and reconcile information across time periods, organizational units, systems, reports, spreadsheets, presentations, and other source formats, including differences in definitions, scope, provenance, and reported values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the quality, completeness, comparability, traceability, and strength of available evidence; document limitations, inconsistencies, unsupported claims, and gaps that affect interpretation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct quantitative, qualitative, and mixed-method synthesis appropriate to the available evidence, including trend analysis, cross-source comparison, portfolio analysis, document and content analysis, and descriptive assessment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive-ready reports, dashboards, visualizations, briefing materials, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate lessons from the 2017–2027 assessment into recommendations for the next strategic planning cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively establish systems and processes for ongoing evidence collection, performance monitoring, data ownership, reporting, and strategic-plan progress reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple workstreams, schedules, milestones, risks, stakeholders, reviews, and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the organization, documentation, governance, and reuse of data supporting strategic planning and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop repeatable and, where practical, automated processes for analysis, dashboarding, and recurring reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with technical, scientific, analytical, operational, and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in data analytics, data science, statistics, public health, health informatics, evaluation, economics, public policy, business analytics, information science, management, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years of progressively responsible experience &lt;/strong&gt;in program evaluation, performance measurement, business intelligence, data analytics, organizational analysis, or a related area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading complex analytical initiatives across multiple organizational units or stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently translate ambiguous leadership questions into analytical approaches, evidence requirements, findings, and executive-level recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collecting, validating, integrating, and interpreting complex quantitative and qualitative information from multiple sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing evaluation frameworks, baselines, or monitoring approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with several analytical methods such as trend analysis, forecasting, benchmarking, portfolio analysis, scenario analysis, or ROI/value analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program and project management skills with experience managing multiple workstreams, schedules, risks, and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Power BI, Tableau, or comparable business intelligence and data visualization tools&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
