&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: large;&quot;&gt;Overview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black Canyon Consulting&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;(BCC)&lt;/strong&gt; is searching for a&lt;strong&gt; User Experience (UX) Developer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to support our work for the National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) at the National Library of Medicine (NLM), an institute of the National Institutes of Health. This is a full-time position located at the NIH campus in Bethesda, MD and/or remote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is part of the National Library of Medicine (NLM) at the National Institutes of Health (NIH).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;NCBI is the world’s premier biomedical center hosting over six million daily users that seek research, clinical, genetic, and other information that directly impacts biomedical research and public health – at NCBI you can literally help to accelerate cures for diseases! NCBI’s wide range of applications, platforms (node, python, Django, C++, you name it) and environments (big data [petabytes], machine learning, multiple clouds) serve more users than almost any other US Government Agency according to &lt;a id=&quot;OWA81049126-8d35-8b03-aebb-3e09d4045a29&quot; class=&quot;OWAAutoLink&quot; href=&quot;https://analytics.usa.gov/&quot; data-auth=&quot;NotApplicable&quot; data-loopstyle=&quot;linkonly&quot;&gt;https://analytics.usa.gov/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We attract the best people in the business with our competitive benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision coverage, 401k plan with employer contribution, paid holidays, vacation, and tuition reimbursement. If you enjoy being a part of a high performing, professional service and technology focused organization, please apply today!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Job Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Database of Human Genotypes and Phenotypes &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gap/&quot;&gt;(dbGaP)&lt;/a&gt; Access team is responsible for developing and maintaining technologies which manage the approval and access to data within the system. The Access team is currently engaged in a UI modernization project encompassing the data access user interfaces, public web site, and approval workflow for the dbGaP systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UI / UX Developer will work as part of the development team to develop and implement new Python and Django UI components and user facing applications defined by the design team into the development, testing, and production environments for the product. This position will also be responsible for collaborating with the development team to integrate these user facing applications into the existing backend components and API’s.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, the developer will be expected to become familiar with the USWDS styling guidelines and leverage best practices to implement styling into the web UI applications. The developer will need to become familiar with NCBI web/application architecture patterns, produce CSS supplements to augment existing NCBI and USWDS CSS templates and produce documentation detailing the applications user workflow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Skills&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing UI / UX applications in a Python / Django framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software development experience in a Linux environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing user facing web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the Agile Scrum development process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: large;&quot;&gt;Benefits and Salary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We attract the best people in the business with our competitive benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision coverage, 401k plan with employer contribution, paid holidays, vacation, and tuition reimbursement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a competitive salary commensurate with experience and the targeted range for this position is $90,000 - $130,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy being a part of a high performing, professional service and technology focused organization, please apply today!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: large;&quot;&gt;Overview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black Canyon Consulting (BCC) is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;User Engagement Lead&lt;/strong&gt; to National Library of Medicine (NLM) in engaging external Unified Medical Language System (UMLS) users to better understand how UMLS and related Health Data Standards are used across the broader Health IT ecosystem. Engagement activities will identify user use cases, needs, dependencies, and perspectives on UMLS data structures, formats, functionality, and complexity. Findings will help NLM better understand current patterns of use and identify opportunities for improvement and modernization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of an organization that operates within the intersection of technology and health, please apply today!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and lead a sustained external UMLS user-engagement program, including outreach strategies, engagement priorities, participant recruitment, interview/listening-session plans, and supporting materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and engage a representative range of UMLS users and stakeholders, including users of UMLS data, terminology resources, APIs, mappings, and related Health IT standards and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct and facilitate interviews, listening sessions, and other structured engagements to understand user workflows, use cases, needs, pain points, dependencies, and perspectives on UMLS data structures, formats, functionality, and complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document user use cases and feedback in a consistent, traceable manner, distinguishing observed needs, dependencies, challenges, and requested capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize qualitative findings across engagements to identify recurring themes, patterns, differences among user communities, and potential areas for UMLS improvement or modernization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with NLM staff and technical or terminology subject matter experts to prepare for specialized engagements and accurately interpret technically complex feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain ongoing relationships and communications with participating UMLS users, including follow-up questions, validation of findings, and additional engagement as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare engagement summaries, findings reports, briefing materials, use-case inventories, and other deliverables that communicate user perspectives clearly to NLM stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track engagement activities, participants, findings, open questions, and follow-up actions while protecting participant information and maintaining appropriate documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development and refinement of repeatable methods, templates, and processes for continued UMLS user engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Experience: Required Knowledge / Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and conducting user research, stakeholder engagement, customer discovery, interviews, listening sessions, or comparable qualitative research activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage technical and non-technical users, ask effective follow-up questions, and translate discussions into clear use cases, findings, and actionable themes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting and coordinating external participants and managing multiple engagements, schedules, follow-up activities, and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong qualitative analysis, synthesis, documentation, facilitation, and written and oral communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical data products and workflows sufficiently to investigate user dependencies, data structures, formats, functionality, and complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Knowledge / Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with UMLS, biomedical terminology, controlled vocabularies, or related Health IT data products and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging technical user communities such as terminology users, informaticians, developers, data engineers, researchers, or health information professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with interoperability, terminology mappings, APIs, FHIR, or other Health IT data-exchange concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting modernization, product discovery, service improvement, or user-centered design initiatives involving complex data products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Education&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BS-level or higher education in health informatics, biomedical informatics, information science, library and information science, public health, social science, user research, communications, healthcare, or a related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is remote-eligible.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: large;&quot;&gt;Benefits and Salary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We attract the best people in the business with our competitive benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision coverage, 401k plan with employer contribution, paid holidays, vacation, and tuition reimbursement.&amp;nbsp;We offer a competitive salary commensurate with experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy being a part of a high performing, professional service and technology focused organization, please apply today!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

